@node D-Bus Roadmap
@section Roadmap

The cmacs D-Bus surface lands incrementally.  Phase 1 (foundations)
shipped in commit @code{ab1bf5f79d3}; the four subsequent phases
follow as separate commits.  None of them break Phase 1 wire
surface.

@subsection Phase 1 --- Foundations (shipped)

@itemize @bullet
@item
Dual bus name claim (@code{org.cmacs.Editor} +
@code{org.cmacs.Editor.Pid@var{N}})
@item
D-Bus session-bus activation file +
@command{make install-cmacs-dbus-service}
@item
@code{org.freedesktop.DBus.ObjectManager} registered at root
@item
@code{org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties} helper with lazy attach
@item
Signal-emit infrastructure (C + Lisp)
@item
File reorg: 838-line monolith split across 8 files in
@file{cmacs/dbus/}
@item
Back-compat: @code{org.cmacs.Editor1} (6 core + 18 gowl methods)
preserved bit-for-bit
@item
12 ERT tests
@end itemize

Five new DEFUNs: @code{cmacs-dbus-start}, @code{cmacs-dbus-stop},
@code{cmacs-dbus-name}, @code{cmacs-dbus-well-known-name},
@code{cmacs-dbus-per-pid-name}, @code{cmacs-dbus-emit-signal},
@code{cmacs-dbus-emit-properties-changed}.

@subsection Phase 2 --- Per-resource objects (planned)

Goal: live entities as observable D-Bus objects.

@itemize @bullet
@item
@code{/org/cmacs/Editor/Buffer/<id>} per live buffer
@item
@code{/org/cmacs/Editor/Frame/<n>} per frame
@item
@code{/org/cmacs/Editor/Window/<n>} per window
@item
@code{/org/cmacs/Editor/Process/<id>} per subprocess
@end itemize

ObjectManager broadcasts @code{InterfacesAdded} /
@code{InterfacesRemoved}; @code{PropertiesChanged} driven by Lisp
hooks.  Per-buffer methods include @code{GetContent () -> h} (memfd
file-descriptor pass), @code{Save ()}, @code{Kill ()},
@code{Revert ()}.

@subsection Phase 3 --- cmacsgi parity (planned)

Goal: every cmacsgi command reachable as a typed D-Bus method.

One file per interface, mirroring @file{cmacs/api/cmacs-api-cmd-*.c}:
@code{Buffer}, @code{File}, @code{Text}, @code{Nav}, @code{Search},
@code{Window}, @code{Config}, @code{Project}, @code{Bookmark},
@code{Clipboard}, @code{VC}, @code{Package}, @code{Monitor} (extracts
gowl), @code{Bar} (extracts gowl), @code{Ripgrep},
@code{Cintrospect}, @code{Cpatch}, @code{Print}.

Long-running operations (compile, grep, rg, package install) get
@code{Request} handles modeled on
@code{org.freedesktop.portal.Request}.

@subsection Phase 4 --- Desktop integration (planned)

@itemize @bullet
@item
@code{org.freedesktop.Application} on root: @code{Activate},
@code{Open}, @code{ActivateAction}
@item
@code{org.gtk.Actions} on root: every interactive defun → typed
action
@item
@code{org.gnome.Shell.SearchProvider2}: buffers / recentf / org-roam
in GNOME shell overview
@item
@code{org.freedesktop.Notifications}: bidirectional --- send via
@code{cmacs-notify} helper, receive via subscription
@item
@code{xdg-desktop-portal} consumer: FileChooser / OpenURI / Print
for sandboxed apps
@end itemize

@subsection Phase 5 --- Creative extensions (planned)

@itemize @bullet
@item
@code{org.freedesktop.login1.Manager.Inhibit}: block sleep when
buffers modified, block idle during long compiles
@item
@code{org.freedesktop.portal.GlobalShortcuts}: desktop-wide hotkeys
that fire even when cmacs isn't focused
@item
@code{org.mpris.MediaPlayer2} server: opt-in mode where mediakeys
navigate buffers
@item
@code{org.cmacs.Editor1.Watch}: observable variable / form watchers
@item
@code{org.cmacs.Editor1.Podomation.Events}: every Pod event becomes
a D-Bus signal
@item
@strong{Shipped:} @code{org.cmacs.Editor1.Events} --- a unified events
endpoint generalizing this idea: a generic @code{Event} firehose plus
typed named signals for file / buffer / project / window / frame /
editor activity (opt-in text and subsystem feeds).  See
@ref{D-Bus Events}.
@item
@code{/org/cmacs/Editor/GI/<Namespace>}: exposes loaded GI
namespaces as typed D-Bus methods.  Turns cmacs into a GI-RPC
bridge reachable from any language.
@end itemize

@subsection Out of scope

@itemize @bullet
@item
System-bus presence (everything stays on session bus)
@item
Cross-machine D-Bus over TCP (use TRAMP / emacsclient over SSH)
@item
KDE StatusNotifierItem (third-party shim via
@code{org.gtk.Actions})
@item
Replacing @command{emacsclient} (both stay)
@item
Migrating cmacsgi off socketpair to D-Bus (FD socketpair faster for
local-child case)
@end itemize

@subsection Versioning and stability

Phase 1 surface is @emph{stable} --- every method, signal, and
property shipped in the foundations release will keep working in
subsequent phases.  New interfaces are additive.  Renames or
removals on existing ifaces would constitute a breaking change and
require a major-version bump (@code{org.cmacs.Editor2}, separate
object hierarchy).
